Package: edge-gaps
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1, libkf6config-bin, systemd
Breaks: tsunyx-launcher (<< 1.7.1)
Enhances: plasma-workspace
Description: invisible screen-edge margins for maximized windows on Plasma Wayland
 Reserves a configurable gap on every screen edge using 1px click-through
 layer-shell surfaces, so maximized windows keep their distance from the
 screen edges and from panels, and floating Plasma panels keep floating.
 Starts automatically in Plasma sessions; configure it in edge-gapsrc.
 .
 Also ships uzunyx-mode, which switches between the normal layout (gaps,
 bottom panel always visible) and a focus mode (no gaps, the bottom panel
 dodges windows). The running edge-gaps re-reads its configuration when
 its "reload" action is activated over D-Bus.
